<title>FRANCE: New York top Q1 originating gateway for Paris.</title>
<headline>New York top Q1 originating gateway for Paris.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top airport gateway for imports to Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>The top ten orignating airport gateways for  ADP imports in January-March 1997, with the percentage change on the same period in 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>     Origin			    Percent</p>
<p>					  Change</p>
<p> 1.  New York	 9,039    down   11.8</p>
<p> 2.  Chicago	  7,223    up	2.2</p>
<p> 3.  Tokyo	    5,493    up     55.7</p>
<p> 4.  Hong Kong	4,691    up     10.4</p>
<p> 5.  Montreal	 4,207    down    9.7</p>
<p> 6.  Los Angeles    3,713    down   11.2</p>
<p> 7.  Singapore	2,442    up     72.9</p>
<p> 8.  Miami	    1,824    down    2.7</p>
<p> 9.  Seoul	    1,780    up     46.3</p>
<p> 10. Casablanca     1,732    down   32.6</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
